"P0" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - BloodofTyrants 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3489863384" "Wardog's Photo"
// tDetailString :
"P1766096719" "Before you left Wardog, he gave you this photo as his last memento. It is of a school, most likely the one where he taught. It reminds you of an experience called...<br><br><color Paragon>Blood of Tyrants</color><br><br>It was the last moments of Wardog's major plan to unleash a Neutron bomb within Nova Praetoria. Things had gone poorly, however; the PPD Test cornered you, Vagabond, and Wardog in the tunnels underneath Nova Praetoria. It was here that you were faced with a choice: fight through the PPD TEST and activate the bomb, killing the entire squad heading down into the tunnels along with Vagabond and Wardog, or betraying the two members of the Resistance to disarm the bomb yourself, earning yourself the title of 'Hero of Praetoria'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P4076726064" "What is going on, {HeroName}? Are they moving the bomb? Where are they planning on letting it loose?"
// Answer Text :
"P126309480" "In Nova, near the Magisterium."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P373436916" "I imagined as such. And they're moving it through the tunnels?<br><br>I've called in a squad of PPD TEST to intercept it, but that doesn't mean that the Resistance can't make it through them.<br><br>{HeroName}, it's up to <i>you</i> to disarm that bomb. There is <i>no</i> question here about what to do or what not to do. We can't risk any innocents being killed by that, <i>any</i>. If that bomb goes off and you're still alive... it will be your final statement that you have truly betrayed all of us here in Praetoria. I hope I'm making myself perfectly clear.<br><br><color yellow>You are the last hope for either all of Nova, or the men in the PPD TEST who are making their way down into those tunnels.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2874555080" "I'll do my best, Marchand. That's all I can promise."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Wardog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3720805120" "Good to see you're here, {HeroName}. The detonator for the Neutron bomb is over there in that crate. You'll be in charge of handling it. Go grab it and we'll get our next plan of action in motion."
// Answer Text :
"P1139723102" "Sounds good."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - BombExpert 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3604738784" "{HeroName}!  We've got a major situation on our hands. I've got the device to disarm the bomb... but I've run into one of those infected Resistance. I've neutralized the disease, but my vision is getting darker and darker..."
// Answer Text :
"P3434773575" "Give me the device. I'll handle disarming the bomb."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P3376799594" "<color orange>You take the device from the bomb expert and look it over. It's actually an extremely simple device, surprisingly so, given the nature of the bomb. You're able to deduce how to easily disarm the bomb. You could do it now, or activate the seers and show <i>all</i> of Praetoria your actions."
// Answer Text :
"P3398636659" "(Activate the seers)"
// Answer Text :
"P3869879023" "(Disarm the bomb)"
// Page SeersActivate Text :
"P3591628685" "<color orange>You use the devices given to you by Beholder and Wardog to activate the seers. Now, all of Praetoria can see what is happening.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P820210874" "(Turn to the seers, explaining the situation)"
// Page Explanation Text :
"P3556717238" "<color orange>You outline the situation for all of Praetoria - about how you infiltrated the Resistance, worked your way into their trust, and that you're now here to disarm the bomb and save everyone's lives.</color>"
// Page BombDisarm Text :
"P3432277079" "<color orange>With a simple push of a button, you disarm the Neutron bomb, stopping what must have been years of planning by the Resistance in one, simple moment.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3498375473" "This is our moment, {HeroName}. We've all worked hard to reach this moment in our history. Can you feel it? The sense that you're standing on the brink of a historical moment? Much like our forefathers before signing the Constitution. We've ensured that most of our operatives will not be in Nova Praetoria. They've also evacuated all of our supporters - very silently, of course. They'll all just know when to <i>not</i> be there.<br><br>All that is left for us is to bring the bomb to the proper location in Nova and unleash it upon the Loyalists. The Seers will ensure that everyone will see the speech I shall give; they will see what happens when a man makes a stand against a group of monsters."
// AcceptString :
"P3494739291" "Where are we bringing the bomb?"
// SendOffString :
"P2816859645" "Through the tunnels of Imperial. We will bring it up through the tunnels in Nova, very close to the Magisterium. And then... it will all be over, {HeroName}. I will make my announcement, with Vagabond at my side. And then, the bomb will let loose, ending the last moments of my cursed life here in Praetoria. I can only hope that people will learn from what I have to say, that I am the last that needs to make this stand. This is my one hope, {HeroName}. Now... let us get moving. We have history to make.<br><br><color yellow>Those Loyalists who have gone undercover would do well to speak with Provost Marchand about events that are happening.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2305401113" "Detonate Neutron Bomb (Single Player)"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2475793122" "We've no time to lose, {HeroName}."
// TaskTitle :
"P109612281" "<color deepskyblue>Blood of Tyrants</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2885683881" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: A Life Long Lived</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4066181690" "You can hear Vagabond and Wardog in the distance of the tunnels. You can feel the pulsing energies of the Neutron bomb, waiting to be released."

